    "turn_text": "You know, when you have excess government spending, and it's almost a type of bribery spending when you borrow stunning amounts of money and then handed out to corporate america now it may have been we wanted a solar factory we wanted to build batteries we wanted to you know even investments in the chip facilities we're benefit beneficiaries of it in arizona but the fact that it's still borrowed money that our kids are going to pay back or your retirement's going to pay back uh... and you know it's It's this perversity of now you see big corporate America leaning towards the Democrats because the Democrats hand them cash. Republicans gave them a more competitive tax code that they had to compete in. In the Democrat world, it's a planned economy. It's industrial policy. Um, you play nice with the Democrats and they write you, you know, a check.",
